# Naming Conventions

Full reference: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md). Stack-specific case rules: [templates/rules/](../../templates/rules/) (enable via [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md)).

## Identifiers

- **English only** for variables, functions, types, files — no Japanese identifiers
- Prefer clarity over brevity; use [abbreviation dictionary](../../doc/coding-conventions.md#略語辞書) only
- **Functions:** verb-first — `getUserById`, `validateInput`
- **Booleans:** `is` / `has` / `can` prefix — `isValid`, `hasError`, `canSubmit`
- **Collections:** plural nouns — `users`, `orderItems`
- **Constants:** `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` with full meaning — `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`

## Forbidden

- Type in names: `strName`, `userList`, `intCount`
- Hungarian notation: `mName`, `s_name`, `opt_value`
- TypeScript: no `I` prefix on interfaces; no leading/trailing `_` for private (use `#` or `private`)
- Meaningless names: `tmp`, `data`, `obj`, `val`
- Test names describing **How** instead of **What**

## Comments

Follow [project-conventions.mdc](./project-conventions.mdc) writing rules:

- Inline/block comments: **Japanese OK**
- Public API JSDoc/docstring: **English** when non-obvious
- Comments explain **Why not** — not what the code obviously does
- Use `TODO:`, `FIXME:`, `NOTE:` annotations

## File naming (TypeScript default)

| Kind | Case | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| General modules | kebab-case | `user-service.ts` |
| React components | PascalCase | `UserProfile.tsx` |
| Tests | kebab-case + `.test.ts` | `user-service.test.ts` |

Python: `snake_case.py`. Go: `snake_case.go`. See stack rules for details.

## Tests

- Include TC ID from `doc/testspec-*.md`
- Name describes expected outcome (**What**), not implementation steps
- Patterns: Vitest `'TC-001: …'`, pytest `test_tc_001_…`, Go `TestTC001_…`
